there are numerous words of Yiddish  origin in English probably because  Yiddish is so expressive but probably  also because of the large Jewish  population in New York City a culturally  influential City a few examples glitch  which means malfunction it comes from  the Yiddish word glitch meaning a slip  shtick which means a gimmick or  performance routine often a comedic one  it comes from schtick meaning an act or  a gimmick but the literal meaning is a  piece or a slice Klutz which means a  clumsy person it comes from clots  literally a block or a lump shmuck which  means a person Unworthy of respect  whether a jerk or a fool it comes from  schmuck which in Yiddish actually refers  to a man's  speaking of a man's  there's the English word schlong which  comes from Yiddish shlang which actually  means snake you can see the connection  Spiel which is like a pitch or someone  trying to sell you on something it comes  from Yiddish Spiel meaning play or game  or the German word Spiel with the same  meaning
 

